29:["$","div",null,{"className":"page_note__G9Hl0","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Posting does not block on the upload: the tile appears in your grid straight away and the transfer runs behind it, and leaving the screen does not kill it. If it fails, the exported files are still on your phone, so retrying re-sends those bytes instead of making you shoot or export again. The clip only becomes a row other people can see once its files have actually landed — a client that dies mid-upload leaves no broken tile in anybody’s feed."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Playback picks one of the three qualities by connection rather than switching mid-stream, and the grid never plays video at all: it draws covers, which is what makes a scroll through it affordable on mobile data."}]]}]
